# D28, open defect of the core (TODO.md § Phase 1 › Défauts ouverts du cœur).
# [B] MC68030UM-1989 §8.1.3 (PDF p. 414): "An address error exception occurs
# when the processor attempts to prefetch an instruction from an odd
# address." Dirk Hoffmann's FBcc/FDBcc (base 863b8d02) test the target with
# misaligned<C>(), false for the 68020 core, and refill the pipe at the odd
# target with no exception (his Bcc/DBcc use misalignedPC and take it); the
# corpus does the same, so these vectors agree with it and are counted open.
@OPEN D28 | fpuraw/identity seed=722 #768
@OPEN D28 | fpuraw/identity seed=722 #1479
@OPEN D28 | fpuraw/off seed=721 #29
@OPEN D28 | fpuraw/off seed=721 #168
