# D29 - EA fields $3D-$3F on the 68030. The fork lets the coprocessor decide
# (a register-to-register operation runs, a memory one clears the status byte
# and takes a Line-F); the oracle's opcode table refuses them outright.
# On Dirk Hoffmann's core (2026-11-24) a valid register-to-register operation
# runs, as the fork's (5 plain lines fail on it); the other 32 plain lines
# take the corpus's Line-F and differ on a descriptor U bit only. The status
# byte question is the @OPEN block below.
fpuraw/identity seed=722 #9
fpuraw/identity seed=722 #27
fpuraw/identity seed=722 #313
